      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would only catch them at the top-level. We would need to recurse to catch nested uses.\n\nThe other issue is that this only catches issues for `var` instructions. You could have an unused function that has a parameter with pointer type that also violates these rules.\n\nSo perhaps we should check these rules in `CheckType()` instead, which is called from all places where a type appears and also already handles the recursion. You\u0027d need to extract the address space from the pointer, but I believe the root type should always be the pointer so that should be doable.",
      "revId": "4113c0110b47c24b66a93c29fd520bddb4be3866",
